  "body": "Follow-up from the refresh of PR #3080 (#2991).\n\nPR #3080 makes the `FirstTraverseLow` refusal name its heights in the frame that the user types in, with the `tilted` flag and the text \"raise the clearance height by at least ... mm\". The verdict `FirstTraverseUnderTable` (#3081) has the same defect: on a tilted plane it names local heights along the tool axis with \"Z\" words (\"lower the clearance plane to Z...\").\n\nThe fix is not only a shift: it needs a new text for a tilted plane, and it moves the pins of #3081 (for example plane 150 becomes 170, and the limit 113.59 becomes 133.59).\n\nWork:\n1. Give `FirstTraverseUnderTable` the user-frame heights and the `tilted` text, as #2991 does.\n2. Update the pins in `crates/app/tests/first_traverse_table.rs`.\n",
